MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Ashes Of The Wake and WAKING THE FALLEN feel like natural next choices because their aggressive vocals and strong guitar riffs fit what I enjoy in In Flames and Soilwork, while still giving me melody to connect with.",
    "Faceless and Iowa connect with the forceful energy I enjoy in Disturbed and my heavier listening, so both feel worth choosing now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Live In Texas misses what I want today because I want to explore a studio album rather than hear a live performance, even if the music itself is related to my interests.",
    "Once puts more emphasis on an orchestral sound than I want right now; I am looking for intensity driven by riffs. Comalies and Fallen appeal to part of my taste, but are less compelling choices for this mood."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat my interest in melodic hard rock as enough reason to choose more of it now, although today I favor the heavier side of my listening.",
    "Sharing a broad connection to heavy music does not make live recordings, orchestral arrangements, and aggressive studio albums equally appealing to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My current choices favor prominent riffs, aggressive vocals, and intensity, especially when those qualities are balanced with melody.",
    "There is a difference between an album fitting my overall taste and my wanting to play it now: I can find Comalies or Reise, Reise appealing while choosing Ashes Of The Wake first."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy and melodic music, but only partly capture my current preference for aggressive, riff-focused studio albums."
}
